# ai_trap.fw -- rules that LOOK mergeable but are not, to test the AI-merge proof.
# Each group invites a merge that would silently change some decisions:
#  - ALLOW ranges split around an exception that sits BETWEEN them in priority
#  - same ports, different protocols
#  - a narrower DENY placed after a broader ALLOW (shadowed for some packets only)
ALLOW TCP FROM 10.0.0.0/8 TO ANY PORT 80-85
DENY  TCP FROM 10.1.0.0/16 TO ANY PORT 80-90
ALLOW TCP FROM 10.0.0.0/8 TO ANY PORT 86-90
ALLOW TCP FROM ANY TO 172.16.0.0/24 PORT 443
ALLOW UDP FROM ANY TO 172.16.0.0/24 PORT 443
DENY  TCP FROM 192.168.7.0/24 TO 172.16.0.0/23 PORT 443
ALLOW TCP FROM ANY TO 172.16.1.0/24 PORT 443
ALLOW TCP FROM ANY TO ANY PORT 8000-8009
DENY  TCP FROM ANY TO ANY PORT 8010
ALLOW TCP FROM ANY TO ANY PORT 8011-8020
ALLOW UDP FROM ANY TO ANY PORT 8000-8020
DENY  ICMP FROM 10.0.0.0/8 TO ANY
ALLOW ICMP FROM ANY TO ANY
DEFAULT DENY
